#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tokens: show how many Claude Code tokens a machine has used, what they cost, and its share of the plan limits.

  tokens                          this machine, last 7 days, by day
  tokens cami                     a mesh machine over SSH (macOS, Linux or Windows)
  tokens --since today --by session
  tokens all                      every machine in one table, with its share of the limits
  tokens win --watch 60           refresh every 60 seconds

Claude Code logs every reply, with its token usage, to ~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl.
tokens reads those logs (over SSH for other machines) and adds them up. Cost is what the
tokens would cost at Anthropic API list prices. The 5-hour and 7-day limits belong to the
account, which every machine shares, so a machine's part of them is estimated from its
share of the API-priced usage of every reachable machine in the same window.
"""

